The contract bundle contains the reviewed locale and API/generated client commits.
Apply it only with the original GW owner's exact source patch from manifest.json.
The composition tree identifies that combination without creating or publishing a
backend commit. The test overlay adds strict assertions to a private copy of the
owner fixture; it does not alter the owner source files.

The production publication flag remains false. Original owners must complete and
qualify catalog-specific activation before a joint release. Earlier cumulative
profiles remain off. The shared Mac release lock and queue still apply.

Full check/build and the focused native protocol results have different scopes.
The manifest and retained logs distinguish real PostgreSQL/TLS tests, controlled
client decoder tests, unrun model/GPU work and the still-open catalogue UI.
